<title>USA: Weather remains hot in W African cocoa areas - WSC.</title>
<headline>Weather remains hot in W African cocoa areas - WSC.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, MASS. 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Weather remains dry and hot in West African cocoa areas but a few very light showers and less heat have eased stress to trees in the Ivory Coast in the past two days, forecaster Weather Services Corp said.</p>
<p>High temperatures are reaching 92-102F and mostly fair and hot weather is forecast for Friday and Saturday with the threat of a few isolated sprinkles in the Ivory Coast on Friday. Temperatures are expected to be above normal.</p>
<p>The outlook is for fair and very warm to hot weather Sunday-Tuesday, with temperatures near to above normal.</p>
</text>
